The point 21°N, 53°W lies in the western North Atlantic, east of the Bahamas and the Caribbean. The area is the western Atlantic abyssal plain, north of the Puerto Rico Trench and south of the Bermuda Rise region. Depths there are typically about 5,000–5,500 m. This is an estimate from general bathymetry rather than a lookup.

Nearby features: the Mid-Atlantic Ridge is far to the east, near 45°W. The Vema Fracture Zone is near 10°N. At 21°N, 53°W the seafloor is likely the Hatteras or Nares Abyssal Plain region, at about 5,300–5,600 m depth. I'll estimate 5,450 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-5450}

