10686.text:
The point (-29, -47) is in the South Atlantic, off the coast of southern Brazil, roughly 500 km east of Florianópolis. That places it over the São Paulo Plateau or the Santos Basin margin, in the deep ocean.

The coast near Florianópolis is at about -48.5 longitude, and the shelf break is around -47.5 to -48 longitude at this latitude. Southeast of there the continental slope descends to the São Paulo Plateau at roughly 2000 to 3000 m depth. At -29 latitude and -47 longitude we are probably on the lower slope or upper rise, perhaps 1500 km from the Rio Grande Rise, which is farther east. I estimate the depth at about 3000 m, and I'm not certain of that figure.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3000}

9569.text:
The point (-17, -121) is in the southeastern Pacific Ocean, west of the East Pacific Rise. The rise crest is near 113-114°W at this latitude, so -121 lies on its western flank, where the seafloor is roughly 3,000-4,000 m deep.

The seafloor at 17°S is shallower near the rise, around 2,800 m at 113°W. Moving west, the crust ages and the depth increases. At 121°W, about 8° from the crest, the crust is about 8° × 111 km × cos(17°) ≈ 850 km away. The Pacific spreading rate there is very fast, about 15 cm/yr in total or 7.5 cm/yr per side, which gives an age of roughly 11 Myr. Depth ≈ 2,600 + 350·√11 ≈ 3,760 m. The nearby Pacific seafloor there is typically about 3,800-4,000 m deep, so I estimate -3,850 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3850}

4753.text:
The point 37.0°N, 33.0°W lies in the North Atlantic, northeast of the Azores. The Azores plateau sits around 25-31°W, and the Mid-Atlantic Ridge crosses near 29-30°W at latitude 37-38°N. The point at 33°W is west of the ridge axis, on the western flank of the ridge. Depths there are about 3000-3500 m. The ridge crest near 36-37°N is shallower, with Azores islands like Flores at 31°W and 39.5°N, and the ridge axis near 34°W at 37°N would be around 2000-2500 m. The Azores triple junction is at about 38.5°N, 28°W, and the ridge axis south of the Azores runs southwest to about 36.5°N, 33.5°W near the Hayes fracture zone region, so 33°W could be near the axis and the flank depth is probably around 2500 m.

I'll estimate about -2800 m.

