The point -45.0, 169.0 is in New Zealand's South Island, in Central Otago. Wanaka is at about -44.7, 169.1, and Lake Dunstan and Cromwell are at about -45.0, 169.2. Lake Dunstan lies near 169.2 to 169.3 E, and Lindis Pass is around -44.6, 169.65. At -45.0, 169.0 we are southwest of Lake Dunstan, near the Pisa Range or the Cardrona area. Lake Wanaka is at -44.5, so it is not a factor here. Lake Hawea is at -44.6. The Pisa Range lies between Lake Wanaka and Cromwell, at roughly 169.0 to 169.2 E and -44.9 to -45.0 S. The Dunstan Range lies to the east of Cromwell. Lake Dunstan sits at 169.2 E, and the Clutha/Kawarau confluence is at 169.2 E, -45.03 S.

At 169.0 E, -45.0 S the terrain is probably in the Pisa Range or the Criffel Range, with elevations of about 1500 m or more. The Kawarau Gorge runs east-west at about -45.0, 169.0 to 169.2, with the river at about 200 m. The Crown Range is at about 168.9 E, -44.9 S. Queenstown is at 168.66 E, so the Remarkables and Cardrona Valley are at about 168.9 E. The point at 169.0 E, -45.0 S is therefore likely just south of the Pisa Range, near the Carrick Range or Nevis. The Carrick Range is at about 169.1 E, -45.05 S, with elevations around 1500 m. I'll estimate about 1200 m.

