Latitude 55.0°N, longitude 127.0°E is in Russia's Amur Oblast, north of the Amur River and near the Tynda region. Tynda sits at about 55.15°N, 124.7°E, so this point is roughly 150 km east of Tynda, in the Stanovoy highlands/Zeya basin area. The Zeya Reservoir lies at about 54.5°N, 127.5°E, and its surface is about 315 m. The point at 55.0°N, 127.0°E is northwest of the reservoir. The reservoir's upper reaches extend north to around 54.8°N, 127.6°E, so the point may be just beyond it on land. The Zeya River flows from the north near 55°N, 127.5°E, so the point is probably in hills at around 500 m.

