Latitude 77.0°N, longitude 149.0°E (assuming positive means east) falls in the Laptev Sea region, near the New Siberian Islands to the east and the Taymyr coast to the west. The Laptev Sea shelf at 77°N, 149°E is open sea north of the Anabar and Lena deltas. The New Siberian Islands lie at about 75°N, 140-150°E, and Kotelny is at about 75.5°N, 141°E. At 77°N, 149°E we are north of those islands, on the outer shelf, with the shelf edge near 78-79°N there. Depth is probably around 100 m.

Bennett Island, in the De Long Islands, is at 76.7°N, 148.9°E, so this point is right on Bennett Island. It is glaciated, with an ice cap reaching about 426 m, and the highest point is around 426 m. The point at 77.0°N is on the northern part of the island, which spans roughly 76.5–76.8°N. Bennett Island's coordinates are about 76°38'N, 148°30'E, and it is roughly 25 km long. So 77.0°N would be just north of the island and likely water. The island's northern tip is about 76.75°N, so 77.0°N is about 25 km off the coast, and the sea depth there is probably around 100 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-110}

