11608.text:
Latitude -39, longitude -3 is in the South Atlantic Ocean, west of Gough Island (40.3°S, 9.9°W) and far from the Tristan da Cunha group. It is also well east of the Mid-Atlantic Ridge, which lies near 14°W at this latitude.

The point sits in the Argentine Basin's eastern region, or possibly on the Agulhas-Falkland side. East of the ridge at 3°W, the Southeast Atlantic seafloor is typically 4000 to 5000 m deep. Near 39°S, 3°W the ridge flank is around 14°W, and the seafloor deepens eastward to roughly 5000 m in the Cape Basin. At 3°W the Meteor Rise and Islas Orcadas Rise are further south (about 50°S), so they are not a factor. I estimate about 4500 m depth, which is a rough guess rather than a looked-up value.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4600}

