Latitude 1.0°N, longitude 141.0°E is in the western Pacific, north of New Guinea. The Papua New Guinea coast at that longitude lies near 2.6°S (Vanimo is around 2.7°S, 141.3°E). So 1°N is about 400 km north of the coast, in open ocean.

The Caroline Basin / Bismarck Sea region lies north of New Guinea. At 1°N, 141°E the depth is roughly 3,000–4,500 m. The Caroline Basin is about 4,000 m deep, and the Sorol Trough and the Eauripik Rise lie further east, near 142–143°E. The Mussau Trench is further south. The seabed near 1°N, 141°E is probably about 4,000 m deep, so I estimate −3,900 m.

