3833.text:
Latitude 47.0, longitude -73.0 is in Quebec, roughly 60 km north of the St. Lawrence River. Trois-Rivières is at 46.35, -72.55, and the Laurentians lie to the north. At 47.0, -73.0 the area is near the Laurentian escarpment, north of Portneuf and west of Quebec City (which is at -71.2). The Saint-Maurice region sits at about -72.7.

Nearby places: Lac-Sergent is at 46.9, -71.8, and Saint-Raymond is at 46.9, -71.8. At -73.0 and 47.0 we are in the Mauricie / Portneuf wildlife reserve area. This is Laurentian plateau terrain with typical elevations of 300–500 m. I'll estimate about 400 m, since the Laurentian Shield there is hilly with many lakes. The chance that the exact point falls on a lake is small, so I'll answer Solid.

