3304.text:
The coordinates 53°N, 51°W lie in the Labrador Sea, off Newfoundland and Labrador. They are roughly 500 km east of the Labrador coast, in the northwest Atlantic. This point is near the Labrador Basin, west of the Greenland–Labrador ridge. The Newfoundland coast is at about 55°W at this latitude, and the Labrador coast is around 56°W. So the point is well offshore, beyond the continental shelf.

Depths here are roughly 3,000–3,500 m. The Labrador Sea basin reaches about 3,500 m in its center near 54°N, 52°W. I estimate about -3,400 m for this point.

