The point 53°N, 31°W is in the North Atlantic, west of the Mid-Atlantic Ridge and east of the Irminger/Newfoundland basin. The ridge axis at 53°N is near 30°W, close to the Charlie-Gibbs Fracture Zone, which lies at about 52–53°N. The ridge crest there is around 28–30°W, so this point is right on the western flank of the ridge near the axis.

Depths near the Charlie-Gibbs fracture zone are about 3000–4000 m. The northern branch of the fracture zone is near 53°N, with a deep trough reaching about 3700–4500 m. At 31°W the seabed is likely on the western flank, at roughly 3000 m depth. I'll estimate -3200 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3200}

7687.text:
