Hanna Shoal is further north at about 72°N, -161°. At 71°N, -165°, the depth is roughly 45 m.


{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-45}

6147.text:
The point (21°N, 125°W) is in the open northeastern Pacific, about 1,500 km west of Baja California and northeast of Hawaii. The seafloor there is abyssal plain, typically around 4,500 to 5,000 m deep. I'm estimating from the general bathymetry of that area rather than a specific chart reading.

