The point (-35, -113) lies in the southeastern Pacific Ocean, west of Chile, and near the East Pacific Rise's flank. The East Pacific Rise at this latitude is around 110-115°W, so the point is close to the crest, which is at roughly 35°S, 111-112°W. Rise crest depths at 35°S are about 2800-3000 m. At 113°W, just west of the crest, the depth would be about 3000 m. The southern East Pacific Rise at 35°S is a fairly shallow, intermediate-spreading ridge, so the depth is probably around -2900 m. At 35°S the crest is near 110.5°W, which puts 113°W about 2.5° west, or roughly 220 km away. The flank depth at that distance would be around 3100 m.

