King William Island spans roughly 68.5–69.8°N and 94–99°W. At -93°, 69°N, the point is east of King William Island. Rae Strait lies at about -94°, and the Boothia Peninsula's western coast runs near -94 to -95° at 69-70°N. At 69°N the Boothia Peninsula is around -95° to -93°, so the point is likely on Boothia land, near Pelly Bay (68.5°N, -89.8°). Felix Harbour lies at about 69.9°N, -93.5°. At 69°N, -93°, the point is probably inland on the Boothia Peninsula, which has many lakes. Elevation is likely about 100 m, and I'll answer Solid.

