Around 41°S the rise crest is near 114°W, so -105 is about 9° east, roughly 800 km. With spreading at about 150 mm/yr, the age is about 5-6 Myr, giving a depth of about 2900-3100 m. Sediment is thin there. The Chile Rise is farther south, so I'll estimate about -3200 m.

