East of Macquarie Island, the Macquarie Ridge and its flanks reach depths of about 4000 to 5000 m. The Hjort Trench lies to the south. At this point the seabed is probably around 4500 m deep, so I estimate -4400 m. This is an estimate from regional bathymetry, not a looked-up value.

