For depth, this area is south of the Chile Rise and the Chile Triple Junction is at about 46.5°S, 75°W. The seafloor at 95°W is on the Nazca/Antarctic plate region, near the Pacific-Antarctic Ridge's northern side. The East Pacific Rise reaches roughly 50°S, 115°W, so at 95°W, 49°S the seafloor is likely abyssal, and the Chile Rise segments around 47°S, 90°W are shallower. Depth is probably about 3500–4000 m. I'll estimate -3900 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3900}

