The Mascarene Basin lies between Madagascar and the Mascarene Plateau, with depths around 4500-5000 m. At 57E, 9S we are probably on the western flank of the plateau, so the depth could be shallower, perhaps 3500-4000 m. The Saya de Malha bank spans roughly 59-62E and 8-12S, and its western edge is near 59E. At 57E the seabed is likely about 4200 m deep.

