The Charlie-Gibbs Fracture Zone is at about 52-53°N, with the ridge crest near 30°W. At 25°W the point is east of the ridge, on the eastern flank. Depths there are about 3,000–3,500 m. The West European Basin starts around 20°W. At 53°N, 25°W the seafloor is likely about 3,300 m deep.

