Latitude -33.0, Longitude 129.0 is in Western Australia/South Australia border region, on the Nullarbor Plain. The Southern Ocean coast is at about -31.7 to -32.0 at this longitude (Great Australian Bight near Eucla at 128.9E, -31.7). So -33.0 is about 140 km south of the coast, which means ocean.

Depth: the continental shelf off Eucla in the Bight is wide. At 33°S, 129°E, the depth is probably around 100-200 m? The shelf edge in the Great Australian Bight is around 34°S at this longitude. The Eucla shelf is wide and shallow, with the shelf break at about 200 m near 33.5°S. At 33.0°S, the depth is likely about 80-100 m. I'll say -90.

