1736.text:
Latitude 71.0, Longitude 53.0 (east) falls in the Barents Sea, east of Novaya Zemlya's southern island? Novaya Zemlya spans roughly 51°E to 69°E. At 71°N the southern island's west coast is near 52–53°E. Matochkin Shar strait is at about 73.3°N, so at 71°N we are on the southern island. Its west coast near 71°N is at about 53°E (Cape Kanin Nos is far south). The southwestern coast of Novaya Zemlya runs from Cape Mauritius (Pakhtusov island) area near 70.5°N, 57°E... Actually Belushya Guba is at 71.5°N, 52.3°E. Because that is on the west coast, 71.0°N, 53.0°E is likely just inland, close to the coast, at a low elevation.

The coast near 71°N lies around 52.5°E, so 53°E is about 15 km inland. Elevation there might be about 100 m.

