Bouvet is at 54.4°S, 3.4°E, so it is far away. The North Scotia Ridge and South Sandwich Trench are well to the west. The Weddell Sea basin starts further south and west. The Mid-Atlantic Ridge runs north-south near 0° to -10° longitude at these latitudes, and the point is likely close to its southern end, where it meets the American-Antarctic Ridge near 60°S, 15°W. The ridge crest depth there is about 3000 to 4000 m, while the surrounding abyssal plains are about 4500 to 5000 m deep. I am placing the point on the flank of the ridge, and I estimate the depth at about -3800 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3800}

