Baikal's southern shore is at about 51.5 N, with the Khamar-Daban rising immediately south of it. At 51.0 N, 105.0 E, I'd estimate the terrain at around 1,500 m. The ridge crest is about 2,000 m. The Khamar-Daban stretches from 51.2 N, 103.5 E to 51.5 N, 107 E, so a point at 51.0 N, 105 E is on the southern side of the crest. Terrain there is perhaps 1,400 m.

