12682.text:
Latitude -51, longitude -15 is in the South Atlantic, west of the Mid-Atlantic Ridge's southern portion. The ridge near 51°S is at about 0 to -5° longitude. At -15° longitude the point lies on the western flank of the ridge, in the Atlantic basin north of the Georgia Basin, with depths around 3500-4000 m.

The ridge axis near 51°S sits around 0°E to -1°E, close to the Bouvet triple junction. The area near the Meteor Rise lies east of 0. At 15°W the flank is about 15 degrees from the axis, which at roughly 17 mm/yr per side corresponds to a crust age of about 40 Myr and a depth of about 3500-4000 m. The Agulhas-Falkland fracture zone is farther north, near 49-50°S. The North Scotia Ridge is far to the west. I estimate -3900 m.

