The coordinates 63.0°N, 87.0°E fall in central Siberia, in Krasnoyarsk Krai. The location is within the Central Siberian Plateau's western part, near the Yenisei basin's eastern side. The Yenisei River is at about 83-86°E at this latitude. At 87°E, 63°N, the area is the Turukhansk/Evenkia region, in the Middle Siberian Plateau's western edge, probably the Podkamennaya Tunguska and Nizhnyaya Tunguska basin, with elevations of roughly 150-300 m. This is a rough estimate, since I'm not certain of the local terrain.

