Latitude 19.0, longitude 9.0 is in northern Niger, in the Sahara near the Termit/Aïr region. The Aïr Mountains lie further east at about 8.5°E, 18°N, so this point is probably just northwest of them. The terrain here is likely a plain with sparse relief, so I estimate an elevation of about 450 m.

Western Aïr is around 8°E, and the Tamesna plain sits near 8°E, 18-19°N at about 400-500 m. At 9°E, 19°N, the area is north of the Aïr, near the Adrar Bous and Temet region. Temet is at about 10°E, 20°N. Elevations there run roughly 500-600 m, so I'll go with 520 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":520}

11083.text:
Latitude -33.0, longitude 27.0 is in the Indian Ocean, off the coast of South Africa near East London. East London sits at about 27.9°E, 33.0°S, so a longitude of 27.0°E is west of it. Port Alfred is at about 26.9°E, 33.6°S, and the coast at 27°E lies near 33.3°S. That puts 33.0°S at 27.0°E inland, roughly 30 km from the coast. The Great Fish River is at about 27.1°E, and Alice is at 26.8°E, 32.8°S. The area is near Peddie, which is at 27.1°E, 33.2°S, with an elevation of around 300 m. So the point is on land.

Estimating the terrain there: Peddie is at about 400 m, and the point is a bit north of it, so I estimate about 450 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":450}

12592.text:
The point is at 49°S, 165°E, in the Southern Ocean southwest of New Zealand. The Campbell Plateau lies southeast of the South Island, and Macquarie Island is near 54.5°S, 159°E. Auckland Islands sit near 50.7°S, 166°E, so this point is north of them and northwest of the Campbell Plateau proper.

West of the Campbell Plateau there is the Macquarie Ridge. At 49°S, 165°E the seafloor is probably on the western edge of the plateau, or in the Solander Trough area, at roughly 1000 to 3000 m depth. The Campbell Plateau is typically 500 to 700 m deep, and its western edge is around 166°E at 49°S. The Emerald Basin lies to the west at about 4000 m depth, and the Macquarie Ridge crest is near 160°E at this latitude. I'm unsure whether 165°E falls on the plateau slope, so I'll estimate a depth of about 1000 m, which is a rough guess.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-1000}

8916.text:
Latitude -9.0, longitude 13.0 falls in Angola. The coast near Cuanza River mouth is at about 13.15°E, -9.3°S, and Luanda is at 13.23°E, -8.84°S. At -9.0, the coastline lies around 13.1–13.2°E, so 13.0°E is probably in the ocean, just offshore.

Checking more closely: south of Luanda, the coast runs from Luanda (13.23, -8.8) to Cabo Ledo (13.25, -9.65), so the coast is at about 13.17°E near -9.0. Longitude 13.0 is therefore about 20 km offshore. The continental shelf there is narrow, with depths around 50–100 m at 20 km out. I'll estimate -80 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-80}

7368.text:
Latitude 9°N, longitude 157°E lies in the western Pacific, north of Pohnpei (about 6.9°N, 158.2°E) and near Pingelap (6.2°N, 160.7°E). Mokil (Mwoakilloa) is at about 6.7°N, 159.8°E, so it is not close. The point is in open ocean, probably on the Ontong Java Plateau's northern margin or in the Caroline Basin.

The Ontong Java Plateau is centered around 1°S to 3°N, 157°E. At 9°N the seafloor is more likely Pacific basin floor, at roughly 4,500 to 5,000 m depth. The Caroline Islands region at 9°N, 157°E is probably in the Caroline Basin or the East Caroline Basin, with depths of about 4,000 to 5,000 m. I'll estimate -4,600 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4600}

572.text:
Latitude 83.0N, longitude -115.0 is in the Arctic Archipelago. Ellef Ringnes Island is at about 78N, Meighen Island at 80N, and Axel Heiberg reaches about 81N. Ellesmere's northern coast is at about 83N but lies near -70 to -90 longitude. At -115 and 83N, the position is in the Arctic Ocean north of the Canadian Arctic Archipelago, beyond Borden Island (about 78.5N) and Prince Patrick Island (about 77N). So this is open ocean, probably over the continental shelf margin or the Canada Basin edge.

The Canada Basin lies west of the Alpha Ridge. At 83N, 115W the area is probably near the Alpha Ridge or the Canadian margin. The Alpha Ridge sits at around 85N, 120W, with depths of about 1500 m. At 83N, 115W the depth is probably about 2000 to 3000 m. The Amundsen Basin and Lomonosov Ridge are on the other side. I'll estimate -2000 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-2000}

2230.text:
Latitude 65.0, longitude -39.0 is in southeast Greenland, roughly 100 km inland from the coast near Ammassalik/Kangerlussuaq. The coast at 65°N lies around -40 to -41°W (Sermilik fjord is at about 65.7N, -38.5W). Ammassalik island is at 65.6N, -37.8W. So at 65.0N, -39.0W we are probably on the coast or just inland, on the edge of the ice sheet.

The coast near 65N runs from about -40.0W at 64.5N up to -39.5W at 65N, so this point is likely inland of the coast, in the ice-sheet margin or in the mountains. The ice sheet margin elevation there is likely around 1500-2000 m. Looking at it further, the Sermilik fjord head is at about 66N, -37.5W. At 65N the coast sits near -40W, and -39W is a bit inland. That is likely mountainous coastal terrain with glaciers, so I estimate about 1600 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":1700}

5520.text:
The point 29.0°N, 61.0°E is in southeastern Iran, in Sistan and Baluchestan province. It lies roughly east of Bam and south of Zahedan, near the Jaz Murian depression to the southwest and the Bampur area to the south. The Taftan volcano is at about 28.6°N, 61.1°E, so this point is just north of it.

The terrain here is a desert plateau at roughly 1000–1400 m. Taftan itself rises to about 3940 m, but the point is about 0.4° (roughly 45 km) north of it, so it sits on the lower plateau. Estimating from the surrounding terrain, I put the elevation at about 1200 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":1200}

9987.text:
