The area is part of the Angola Basin and Cape Basin region, where abyssal depths are typically 4,500 to 5,500 m. The Walvis Ridge lies further north at about 20-30°S, running from the Namibian coast toward Tristan da Cunha. At 21°S the ridge is near the coast, around 5-10°E, so it is not at -5°. At -5° longitude we are east of the Mid-Atlantic Ridge, on the flank, where depths are around 4,000 to 5,000 m. The ridge crest at 20°S is near 13°W, with flank depths increasing eastward, so about 4,500 m is reasonable at 5°W.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4600}

13177.text:
The point is at 57°S, 105°W, in the southeastern Pacific Ocean. That area lies west of the Chile Rise and south of the Easter Island region, and it sits near the East Pacific Rise's southern extension, which is the Pacific-Antarctic Ridge. The Pacific-Antarctic Ridge runs from about 55°S, 140°W toward the Chile Triple Junction near 46°S, 76°W. So the ridge is roughly at 57°S, 115°W or so, and 105°W would be a bit off the ridge axis.

The Eltanin fracture zone is around 57°S, 145°W, so it is not nearby. The seafloor near 105°W is probably about 3,000 to 3,500 m deep, since the ridge crest there is shallower, around 2,500 to 3,000 m. I estimate about -3,300 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3300}

3374.text:
Latitude 53.0 N, longitude 89.0 E is in southern Siberia, in Khakassia or Krasnoyarsk Krai near the Altai and Sayan region. Longitude 89 E at latitude 53 N is roughly north of the Sayan Mountains, near the Abakan area (Abakan is at 91.4 E). A spot at 89 E sits in the western part of Khakassia, near Tashtyp or the Kuznetsk Alatau foothills, or in the Altai Republic. This is probably low mountains with an elevation of around 500-1000 m.

Taking the Abakan steppe at about 300-400 m, and the Sayan foothills to the west rising higher, 89 E, 53 N is probably near the Ak-Sug/Tashtyp area. I estimate about 700 m.

