The shelf break in the Laptev region is at about 78-79N, with depths near 100-500 m at the edge. At 79N, 145E the shelf edge is plausible, so the seabed is probably around 300 m deep, perhaps more. IBCAO shows the Laptev shelf break at roughly 80N at 130E, and further east near 79N at 145E the shelf is about 80-100 m deep to the north of the De Long Islands. The slope begins around 78-79N to the east at 150E. I'll estimate -400 m.

