Latitude -11, longitude -11 lies in the South Atlantic Ocean. It is west of Africa (Angola coast is at about 13°E) and northwest of St Helena, which is at about -15.9, -5.7. The location is near the Mid-Atlantic Ridge region, but the ridge axis at this latitude is around -13°W. Around 11°S, the ridge axis is near 13°W, so -11 lies on the eastern flank of the ridge, probably 3,000–4,000 m deep.

The ridge crest at this latitude sits at about 2,500–3,000 m depth. About 2° east of the axis, the flank would be roughly 3,200 m deep. I estimate -3300 m.

