Seafloor age here is about 15 Ma, and the area is near the East Pacific Rise flank, which puts depths around 3,500 to 4,000 m. The Orozco and Clipperton fracture zones are not close. Most seafloor near 13°N, 101°W is about 3,600 m deep, so I'll estimate -3600 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3600}

9263.text:
