The Walvis Ridge lies further south, around -20 to -26. At -19 the margin slopes gradually into the Angola Basin, which is deeper than 3000 m. Shelf-edge depth near Cunene at -17.3 is about 200 m. At -19 the coast is at about 12.5E, so 11E is about 1.5 degrees (about 160 km) offshore. The shelf is about 100 km wide there, so this point is just past the break. I estimate a depth of about -700 m.

