{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4900}

3249.text:
Latitude 53.0 N, longitude -161.0 W lies south of the Alaska Peninsula. Unimak Island is near 54.8 N, 164 W, and the Shumagin Islands are near 55 N, 160 W. At 53 N, 161 W we are about 250 km south of the peninsula, in the Pacific, south of the Aleutian Trench's northern edge.

