The seafloor here is part of the Australian-Antarctic Basin, or possibly near the Southeast Indian Ridge's eastern end. The ridge runs from about 140°E at 62°S toward the Macquarie Triple Junction near 62°S, 161°E. At 153°E the Southeast Indian Ridge sits around 60–62°S, with depths about 2500–3500 m. The Pacific-Antarctic Ridge begins at the triple junction. The point is therefore likely near the ridge axis, with a depth of around 3000 m, though the nearby abyssal plain would be about 4000 m. I'll estimate -3300 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3300}

