{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4500}

3481.text:
Latitude 51.0, longitude -57.0 falls in the Gulf of St. Lawrence region, near the Strait of Belle Isle and the Quebec Lower North Shore. Newfoundland's Northern Peninsula sits at about 51°N, 56-57°W. The tip near Pistolet Bay is around 51.4°N, 55.8°W, and the west coast of the peninsula runs near 57°W at about 50°N, so 51.0°N, 57.0°W is probably in the Gulf. The Quebec coast near Blanc-Sablon is at 51.4°N, 57.1°W, and the Lower North Shore near Brador is around 51.5°N, 57.8°W. The point at 51.0°N, 57.0°W is therefore about 40 km south of the Quebec coast, in the Strait of Belle Isle's western approach, with the Newfoundland coast at about 51.0°N, 56.8°W near Flowers Cove. Flowers Cove is at 51.3°N, 56.7°W and Port au Choix at 50.7°N, 57.4°W. At 51.0°N the coast would be about 57.1°W, near Sandy Cove/Eddies Cove, so the point is probably just offshore, in shallow water of roughly 20-50 m depth.

I'll answer Water with an elevation of about -40 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-40}

809.text:
The point is at 81.0°N, 1°W, which lies in the Arctic Ocean north of Greenland and east of Peary Land. It is near the Greenland Sea and Fram Strait, northeast of Greenland's coast. The Greenland coast at this longitude is around 83°N, so 81°N, 1°W is well offshore. This area is the Greenland continental margin, north of the Greenland Sea.

