The Gakkel Ridge near 85-87°N, 60-90°E reaches about 3500-4000 m deep. At 87°N, 95°E, the Lomonosov Ridge is on the opposite side of the pole, near 140°E and 175°W, so this point is likely in the Amundsen Basin at about 4200 m deep. I estimate about -4100 m.

