3421.text:
The point 51.0°N, 177.0°W lies in the Aleutian region. The Aleutian Islands near 51°N include the Delarof Islands at about 179°W and Adak at 176.6°W, 51.8°N. Tanaga is at 178°W, 51.9°N, and Kanaga is at 177.2°W, 51.9°N. So 51.0°N is roughly 50 miles south of Adak, which puts it in the Pacific south of the Aleutian arc.

The Aleutian Trench lies south of the islands. Near 177°W the trench axis is around 50°N or slightly south, and its depth is about 6,000 m or more. On the Pacific side the slope descends from the islands steeply. At 51°N, about 100 km south of Adak, the depth is probably 4,000–5,000 m. The trench axis near 175°W is at about 50.5°N, and the depth there is about 7,000 m. At 177°W the trench is at about 50.3°N, perhaps 7,000 m deep. At 51.0°N I estimate about 5,000 m, since the point is on the lower slope, and I will report that.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-5000}

