{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-5450}

4097.text:
The point 45.0°N, 95.0°E is in western Mongolia, in the Gobi-Altai region. It lies south of the Altai range and near Bayankhongor/Govi-Altai province. Terrain around there is probably 2000 m or so.

More specifically, Mongolia's Gobi-Altai province contains Altai city at about 46.4°N, 96.3°E, at roughly 2200 m. A point at 45°N, 95°E is southwest of that, near the Gobi-Altai ridges. The Atas Bogd mountain is at about 44.5°N, 94.5°E. The area between the Gobi Altai ranges has basins at about 1500 to 2000 m. Estimating about 1900 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":1900}

6105.text:
Latitude 23.0°N, longitude 151.0°E lies in the western Pacific, east of the Mariana Islands and north of the Marshall Islands. The area is likely the Pacific abyssal plain in the Northwest Pacific Basin, near the Magellan Seamounts and Wake Island region. Wake is at 19°N, 167°E, and the Marcus-Wake seamounts run around 20-25°N, 150-170°E. Longitude 151°E at 23°N is just east of the Mariana Ridge, which sits at about 145°E, and the West Mariana Ridge is near 138°E. The Pigafetta Basin is around 16°N, 150°E, with a depth of about 5,800 m.

