{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-5600}

11595.text:
The point at 39°S, 29°W is in the South Atlantic, west of the Mid-Atlantic Ridge. The ridge axis near 39°S sits at roughly 13–15°W, and the Rio Grande Rise lies further north-west at about 30°S, so this point is not on it. It falls in the Argentine Basin's eastern side, or on the flank of the ridge. Seafloor depths there are around 4500–5000 m.

The Mid-Atlantic Ridge at this latitude is near 14°W, and the Tristan hotspot track is further east, so 29°W is about 15° of longitude west of the axis. At a spreading rate of about 3.5 cm/yr per side, that distance corresponds to crust roughly 45 million years old. Such crust lies at about 4500 m depth, so I estimate around -4600 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4600}

3098.text:
Latitude 55.0, longitude -103.0 is in northern Manitoba/Saskatchewan border region. The Manitoba-Saskatchewan border is at about -102°, so -103 lies in Saskatchewan, near Reindeer Lake's south end? Reindeer Lake is at 57°N. At 55N, -103 is near Amisk Lake, Deschambault Lake (54.8N, -103.8), Namew Lake (54.0N, -102.5), and Sturgeon-weir River. Churchill River region near Pelican Narrows (55.17N, -102.93) — Pelican Narrows is on Mirond Lake and Opawikscikan Lake. So the point is likely close to Pelican Narrows, in the Canadian Shield with many lakes. Elevation of the area is about 300 m. Lakes there are around 300 m; Mirond Lake is about 303 m.

The point at 55.0, -103.0 is about 20 km south of Pelican Narrows. It could be land at around 300 m, so I'll say solid at 305.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":305}

6804.text:
Latitude 15.0 N, longitude 109.0 E is in the South China Sea, east of Vietnam's coast. The Vietnamese coast near Quang Ngai (15.1 N) sits at about 108.8 E. The point at 109.0 E is therefore about 20 km offshore, just east of the coast.

The coast at 15 N is around 108.8 E. Near Ly Son Island (15.38 N, 109.15 E), the water depth is about 50 m. At 15.0 N, 109.0 E the shelf depth is probably around 40-60 m. I'll estimate -50 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-50}

2448.text:
Latitude 63.0 N, longitude 37.0 E is in northwestern Russia, in the Arkhangelsk Oblast / Karelia area. Karelia sits at roughly 61-66 N and 30-37 E, and the White Sea coast is further north at about 64-66 N. At 63 N, 37 E the point is probably in the southern Arkhangelsk Oblast, near Onega or Plesetsk, so it is land.

Lake Onega's eastern shore lies near 35.5 E, so 37 E is east of the lake. The terrain there is the Onega-Northern Dvina watershed, with elevations of about 100-150 m. I estimate 130 m.

