3810.text:
The coordinates 47.0°N, 119.0°W fall in central Washington State, in the Columbia Basin. That puts them near Ephrata and Moses Lake. Moses Lake is at about 47.13°N, 119.28°W and Ephrata at about 47.32°N, 119.55°W. The point at 47.0, -119.0 is south of Moses Lake and east of the Columbia River, around the Potholes Reservoir and the Othello area. Potholes Reservoir sits at about 46.97°N, 119.3°W, so the point is east of it.

The terrain there is the channeled scablands, with Lind Coulee and Crab Creek nearby. Elevation in the area is roughly 350-400 m. I'm estimating about 380 m from the surrounding landscape, not from a lookup, and I'm treating the point as land.

