The Brazil Basin lies west of the ridge, at roughly 5,000 m depth. At 27°W the seafloor is about 60 to 70 Myr old, which suggests a depth near 4,500 m. I'll estimate -4300 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4300}

14127.text:
Location: 67°S, 5°W is in the Weddell Sea sector off Antarctica's Queen Maud Land coast. The coast near 5°W lies around 70°S, where the Fimbul Ice Shelf is at about 3°W to 3°E and the Jelbart Ice Shelf is near 8°W. At 67°S the point is in open ocean, north of the coast by about 3 degrees.

The seabed there is likely in the Weddell Sea basin or on the Maud Rise flank. Maud Rise is centered at about 65°S, 3°E, with depths of about 2000-3000 m. At 67°S, 5°W the depth is probably around 4500 m, since the abyssal plain of the Weddell Sea is at about 4500-5000 m. The Astrid Ridge is farther east, so I'll estimate -4400 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4400}

4714.text:
Latitude 37.0, longitude -111.0 is in northern Arizona, near the Utah border. It lies east of Kayenta, in the Navajo Nation near Monument Valley, which is about 36.98 N, 110.1 W. Kayenta itself is at 36.73 N, 110.25 W. At -111.0 the point is west of Kayenta, near Navajo Mountain's east side, close to the Rainbow Bridge area.

Navajo Mountain is at 37.03 N, 110.87 W. Lake Powell's San Juan arm runs near 37.1 N, 111.0 W, though the lake is probably not at exactly 37.0. The point at 37.0, -111.0 is south of the San Juan arm, in the Paiute Mesa and Skeleton Mesa area, at an elevation of roughly 1800 m. The lake's San Juan arm sits at about 37.08 N, 110.9 W, and Rainbow Bridge at 37.077 N, 110.964 W. So 37.0, -111.0 is about 8 km south of Rainbow Bridge, which puts it on the plateau south of Forbidding Canyon, toward Navajo Canyon. The terrain there is about 1700 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":1750}

1363.text:
Latitude 75.0°N, longitude 27.0°E lies in the Barents Sea, east of Svalbard's Edgeøya and southeast of Spitsbergen. Svalbard spans roughly 76.5–80°N, so 75°N is south of it. Bear Island is at 74.4°N, 19°E, which is also well to the west. The point is therefore open sea in the Barents Sea, north of the Bear Island trough and east of the Spitsbergenbanken.

