The Kerguelen Plateau lies further north at about 60°E, but it is mostly north of 60°S. Around 65°S, 61°E, the seafloor is probably the continental rise or the abyssal plain at about -3500 to -4000 m. The shelf break near Prydz Bay's western side lies at about 66-67°S. The continental slope at 65°S is probably around -2500 to -3500 m, so I'll estimate -3400 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3400}

2381.text:
Latitude 63.0, Longitude -97.0 is in Nunavut, Canada, west of Hudson Bay. Rankin Inlet is at about 62.8N, 92.1W, and Baker Lake is at about 64.3N, 96W. The point is inland, southwest of Baker Lake, near Kaminak Lake, which lies around 62.2N, 95.0W. Chesterfield Inlet is at about 63.3N, 90.7W. Wager Bay is farther east.

