Abyssal plains in this area are typically about 3500–4000 m deep. The East Pacific Rise is farther east, near 106°W, so the seafloor at 117°W is older and deeper. I estimate about -3800 m, based on regional depth patterns rather than a specific lookup.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3800}

2223.text:
Location: 65.0°N, 53.0°W is in southwest Greenland. Nuuk is at 64.17°N, 51.7°W. Fjords around there: Godthåbsfjord runs from Nuuk inland to the northeast. At 65°N, 53°W, the coast is around 52°W at that latitude, so this point is about 0.8° of longitude (~38 km) west of the coast, which puts it offshore in Davis Strait on the continental shelf.

Depth on the shelf there is about 100-300 m. Near Fyllas Bank (64°N, 53.5°W) depths are ~50-100 m. At 65°N, 53°W, the area is probably the shelf off Maniitsoq/Nuuk, with a depth of maybe 150 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-150}

