The Carlsberg Ridge is much farther south, and the Murray Ridge is at about 23°N, 60°E, so neither affects this point. The Indus Fan fills the northern Arabian Sea, and the Arabian Basin floor near 19°N, 65°E is about 3,400 m deep. I'm estimating from memory of the regional bathymetry, so the depth is approximate.

