The shelf there is roughly 100 km wide, and the shelf break is at about 2°S. At 1°S the point is probably on the upper continental slope or the edge of the Ceará Plateau region. The slope off the Amazon/Pará-Maranhão margin falls from about 100 m to over 3000 m. The coast near 44°W is at about 2.5°S. At 41°W the coast is at about 3°S, and the point is 2° of latitude, about 220 km, offshore, so it is beyond the shelf, probably on the slope at about 2000–3000 m depth. I'll estimate -3000 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3000}

