5395.text:
Latitude 31°N, longitude 171°E lies in the northwest Pacific Ocean, east of Japan and south of the Emperor Seamounts. The area is open ocean on the Pacific Plate, where seafloor depths are typically around 5,500 to 6,000 m. I have no specific bathymetry for this exact point, so I am estimating from that regional depth.

The Mariana Trench and the Marcus-Wake seamounts lie farther south and west, and the Wake Island region is at about 19°N, 167°E. At 31°N, 171°E the seafloor is probably abyssal plain, so I estimate about -5,600 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-5600}

