The continental shelf edge in the Amundsen Sea is near -72 to -73. At -69 the depth is probably the abyssal plain or lower rise, around 4,000 to 4,500 m. I'll estimate -4300 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4300}

15444.text:
Latitude -81, longitude 109 is in East Antarctica, near Vostok Station, which sits at about -78.46, 106.83. At -81, 109 the point is south-southeast of Vostok, on the high plateau. The ice surface there is roughly 3,300 to 3,500 m. Dome A is far to the west, and the region south of Vostok has surface heights around 3,400 m.

