6531.text:
The point 17.0°N, 77.0°W lies in the Caribbean Sea, south of Jamaica. Jamaica's southern coast is around 18°N, so this point is about 100 km south of it, in the Jamaica Channel / Colombian Basin region. The Pedro Bank lies near 17°N, 77.5°W, so the point is close to its southeastern edge. Pedro Bank is shallow, roughly 20-50 m deep, and spans about 17.0–17.5°N and 77–78.5°W. The southern edge of the bank is around 16.9°N.

East of 77.5°W the bank's edge is more complex, and at 77.0°W the point is probably off the bank's eastern part, where the Jamaica–Pedro channel is deep. The Pedro Bank's eastern end is near 77.0°W at about 17.1°N, and there are cays at Pedro Cays near 17.0°N, 77.8°W. The area south of Jamaica between 17 and 18°N at 77°W includes the Pedro Channel, which is several hundred meters to over 1000 m deep. Since the point sits near the bank's slope, I'll estimate about -600 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-600}

14702.text:
