At 65°E and -73°, I think the point falls on the grounded ice plateau west of the Lambert Glacier, in the Mawson Escarpment and Prince Charles Mountains area. The Mawson Escarpment sits around 62-63°E at -73°. Just east of it, at 65°E, the surface is probably an ice plateau at about 2000 m. The Lambert Glacier main trunk is around 70°E, so 65°E is likely on the flank, possibly near the Fisher Glacier and Mount Menzies, which is at 61°E, -73.5°. The Charles Mountains region near 66°E, -72° has an ice surface at about 1500-2000 m. I'll estimate 1900 m.

{"type":"Solid","elevation_m":1900}

13036.text:
Latitude -55, longitude -27 lies in the South Atlantic, north of the South Sandwich Islands (which sit near 56-59°S, 26-28°W). The point is roughly 55°S, 27°W, in the Atlantic west of the South Sandwich arc, within the Georgia Basin / East Scotia Sea area.

The South Sandwich Islands start at about 56.3°S (Zavodovski), so the point is just north of the arc. The East Scotia Sea back-arc basin lies west of the arc, with depths of about 3000-4000 m. The point is at 27°W, which is on the north side of the arc, and the trench lies east of the arc at about 24-25°W. North of the arc at 55°S, 27°W, the seafloor is likely about 3000 m deep. Between the South Georgia and South Sandwich islands, depths are around 3000-4000 m, so I estimate -3300 m.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-3300}

