The Oates Land coast runs from about 153 E to 160 E, with the coastline near 69-70 S. At 159 E, 67 S is therefore about 300 km offshore in the open Southern Ocean. The Southern Ocean there is deep, with abyssal depths around 3000 to 4000 m. The continental slope is near 66 S and the rise lies beyond it. The Wilkes Land margin at 159 E has a coast near 69 S and a shelf edge around 66 S, so 67 S is probably on the slope or shelf edge, with a depth of roughly 2500 m. I'll estimate -2800.

