Latitude 77.0°N, longitude -25.0° lies off the northeast coast of Greenland, on the Greenland Sea/Northeast Greenland shelf. Greenland's coast near 77°N is around -18° to -20° longitude (Kronprins Christian Land is at about 80°N, and Dove Bugt at about 77°N, -20°). Shelf waters extend out to about -10° to -15° in the east, but the coast here lies to the west of that. At -25° longitude and 77°N we are inland, over the Greenland Ice Sheet's northeastern part. Looking at the geography, Store Koldewey is at about 76.4°N, -18.5°. Kejser Franz Joseph Fjord is at 73°N, -25°. Around 77°N, -25° is probably Wollaston Forland/Hold with Hope, but that's at -19° to -20°. Further west at -25° is the Dronning Louise Land area (about 76.5°N, -25°), which is ice-covered at an elevation of about 1000 m or more. Ice sheet elevations in this area are about 1000–1500 m.

