{"type": "Water", "elevation_m": -4000}

15047.text:
Latitude -77, longitude 35 is in East Antarctica, in Queen Maud Land / Dronning Maud Land. This is inland, south of the coast, which lies around -70 at that longitude. The Shirase/Jelbart area is further west. At 35°E, -77°, I am near the Wohlthat/Orvin mountains region? Those are around 10-15°E. Around 35°E, 77°S the ice sheet is a high plateau, with surface elevation probably around 3000 m. Nearby Dome Fuji is at 39.7°E, 77.3°S, with surface elevation 3810 m. So 35°E, 77°S is close to Dome Fuji, at roughly 3700 m.

The ice surface there is likely about 3700 m.

