The seafloor in this part of the Pacific is probably abyssal plain at about 4,800–5,200 m depth. The area lies near the Line Islands Ridge and east of the Penrhyn basin. Seafloor in the Central Pacific Basin near the equator is around 4,900 m, so I'll use -4950.

{"type":"Water","elevation_m":-4950}

2051.text:
