The Transantarctic Mountains and the Ross Ice Shelf lie along 180° to 150°W. At 137°W the direction is toward Marie Byrd Land and the Ross Ice Shelf edge. The Ross Ice Shelf is reached at around 85°S, so 89°S is still on the polar plateau, with a surface of about 2700 m. Using a pole value of 2835 m and a slight decrease toward the Ross side, I estimate about 2750 m.

