The seabed there lies on abyssal plain north of the Clipperton Fracture Zone. The crust is roughly 40 million years old or more, and abyssal depths in this region are typically about 4,000 to 5,000 m. I estimate a seabed elevation of about -4,300 m. This is an estimate from regional depth patterns, not a looked-up value.

