15379.text:
Latitude -81, longitude -21 is in the Weddell Sea sector of Antarctica. This location is in the Filchner Ice Shelf region, or just next to it. The Filchner-Ronne ice shelf front sits around 78°S, and the Filchner ice shelf extends south to about 80-81°S at longitudes of -30 to -40. At -21°, 81°S, this is probably the Coats Land / Theron Mountains area, where the Slessor Glacier flows. The Theron Mountains lie around 79°S, 28°W. The Shackleton Range is at 80.5°S, 25°W. So -81, -21 is just east of the Shackleton Range, in the inland ice of Slessor Glacier / Recovery Glacier area. This is grounded ice with a surface elevation of roughly 1000 m.

