4738.text:
The point 37°N, 63°W lies in the western North Atlantic, south of Nova Scotia and southeast of Cape Cod. It is east of the Gulf Stream's western portion and near Bermuda's northwest. Bermuda is at 32.3°N, 64.75°W, so the point is about 5° north of it. This is the Sargasso Sea region, on the abyssal plain, roughly south of the New England Seamounts, which run along about 38–40°N and 60–67°W.

The Nashville and Gosnold seamounts lie near 35–38°N. The Bermuda Rise sits at about 33°N, with depths around 4,500–5,000 m. The Sohm Abyssal Plain lies north of this, at about 5,000 m, and at 37°N, 63°W I estimate a depth of about 5,000 m.

