Latitude -43, longitude 103 is in the southeastern Indian Ocean, southwest of Australia. The area lies south of the Southeast Indian Ridge's northern portion, roughly between the Broken Ridge and the Southeast Indian Ridge. The Southeast Indian Ridge runs through about -43 near longitude 90-100 and continues southeast. At longitude 103 the ridge is near latitude -42 to -46, so the depth is probably about 3000-3500 m on the ridge flank. The Amsterdam-St Paul plateau lies at about 78E, so it is not relevant here. The Australian-Antarctic Discordance is at about 120E.

