Latitude -85, longitude 43 lies in East Antarctica, south of Dronning Maud Land, near the Pensacola Mountains and the Recovery Glacier area. The Pensacola Mountains are at about 83-85°S and 50-60°W, so they are not at this longitude. At 43°E and 85°S the point is on the interior plateau, in the region toward the Dome Argus side, and the surface elevation there is probably around 2800-3200 m. The Recovery Glacier catchment lies near 80-82°S and 20-30°W, so it is also far from this point.

